  { p: 'Which of these popular ideas about the emperors is contradicted by Tacitus, the most cautious source on the fire of 64?', op: ['That Caligula planned to make his horse consul', 'That Nero was in Rome playing the lyre while the city burned', 'That Nero blamed the Christians for the fire', 'That Commodus fought in the arena'], certa: 1, exp: 'Tacitus says Nero was at Antium and returned to organise relief; Suetonius and Dio mention a song during the fire, but the scene of the lyre in Rome is a later elaboration.' }
